      "path": "20 论文/chuaDeepReinforcementLearning2018",
      "title": "Deep Reinforcement Learning in a Handful of Trials using Probabilistic Dynamics Models",
      "type": "paper",
      "citekey": "chuaDeepReinforcementLearning2018",
      "status": "inbox",
      "readingLevel": "",
      "paperRole": "",
      "atlasLabel": "",
      "year": 2018,
      "authors": "Kurtland Chua, Roberto Calandra, Rowan McAllister, Sergey Levine",
      "topics": [
        "vla"
      ],
      "created": "2026-10-10",
      "readDate": "",
      "doi": "10.48550/arXiv.1805.12114",
      "sourceUrl": "http://arxiv.org/abs/1805.12114",
      "zoteroUri": "zotero://select/library/items/ERJ3IUYW",
      "noteDensity": 0,
      "evidenceCount": 9,
      "maturity": 27,
      "atlasCardHtml": "<p><img src=\"/images/atlas-cards/paper-4f65b66851-8f2786ed072a.png\" alt=\"截屏2026-10-10 16.02.12\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" /></p>\n<ol>\n<li>MBRL is appealing because the dynamics model is reward-independent and therefore can generalize to new tasks in the same environment, and it can easily benefit from all of the advances in deep supervised learning to utilize high-capacity models.</li>\n<li>高斯过程GP：非参数，输出分布；不确定性很可靠；适合小样本低维；大数据计算成本高</li>\n<li>PET出发点：普通神经网络小数据下容易过拟合，导致远期预测不可靠，于是选择保留神经网络的高表达能力，同时用概率输出和ensemble补充不确定性估计（恰当地把不确定性纳入动力学模型） //当年的dropout方法也是表现不确定性的一种方式</li>\n<li>偶然不确定性和认知不确定性</li>\n<li>总结：论文通过提出了一个新框架，巧妙地处理了偶然不确定性和认知不确定性之间的关系，实现了MBRL既可以省数据，又能达到较好的最终效果</li>\n</ol>",
      "atlasCardImages": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "paper-fc15e3571d",
      "path": "20 论文/haWorldModels2018",
      "title": "World Models",
